{"raw": {"https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1336?c=uis": {"title": "Program Coordinator, Academic Governance and Institutional Effectiveness", "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Program Coordinator, Academic Governance and Institutional Effectiveness Springfield, IL, United States | 1005197 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Program Coordinator, Academic Governance and Institutional Effectiveness | Job Details Program Coordinator, Academic Governance and Institutional Effectiveness Posting Category: About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu and the unit web page at https://www.uis.edu/oire. Application deadline: 10/19/2026 Minimum Starting Salary: $32.30 per hour/7.5 hour day Job Summary: The Program Coordinator for Academic Governance and Institutional Effectiveness administers UIS' institution-wide academic governance function within the Office of Institutional Research and Effectiveness. Working under general supervision, the position serves as the university's resource for the policies, approval pathways, documentation standards, and external requirements governing academic programs, courses, units, and related academic actions. The coordinator manages interconnected governance processes from initial consultation through final institutional and external action; advises academic and administrative stakeholders; interprets and applies university, system, state, federal, and accreditor requirements; and maintains the authoritative records and resources that support consistent decision-making. The position also coordinates implementation of approved curricular actions across the academic codebook, catalog, institutional inventories, and compliance records. Through this work, the coordinator supports the integrity of shared governance, institutional compliance, and timely execution of academic priorities. This is an on-campus position. Duties & Responsibilities: Administer the Academic Governance Functional Area: Coordinate the university-wide review and approval portfolio for new and revised academic programs, courses, units, and other academic actions from proposal development through final implementation.\u00a0 Establish and manage annual governance calendars, workflow controls, documentation standards, forms, guidance, and status-tracking processes. Monitor proposals across multiple review bodies and approval levels; identify incomplete or inconsistent submissions, resolve process issues, and communicate required actions and deadlines to stakeholders. Maintain the UIS Levels of Governance resource as the authoritative operational guide to required review levels and sequencing. Provide Program Expertise, Policy Interpretation, and Consultation: Serve as the primary resource for academic governance procedures, approval pathways, documentation requirements, and implementation timelines. Interpret and apply University Statutes, Board of Trustees requirements, University of Illinois System policies, UIS governance procedures, Illinois Board of Higher Education expectations, Higher Learning Commission requirements, and other applicable standards. Advise faculty, program directors, chairs, deans, governance bodies, and Academic Affairs leaders on the design, documentation, routing, and implementation of academic actions. Develop training, procedural guidance, templates, and other resources that promote consistent and compliant governance practices across academic units. Administer Academic Codebook, Records and Catalog Implementation: Administer the UIS academic codebook and coordinate catalog implementation resulting from approved curricular and organizational actions. Maintain institutional academic governance records, historical documentation, approval evidence, and institutional inventories of academic programs and units. Reconcile information across governance, catalog, codebook, accreditation, and reporting systems; investigate discrepancies and coordinate corrective action. Produce status reports, analyses, and management information to support academic planning, compliance, and institutional decision-making. Coordinate Institutional and External Approvals: Prepare and author academic agenda items and supporting materials for submission to the Board of Trustees and external entities. Coordinate the preparation, submission, tracking, revision, and retention of materials required by the University of Illinois System Office, Board of Trustees, Illinois Board of Higher Education, Higher Learning Commission, and other external entities. Represent UIS, as assigned, in system-level meetings concerning academic approval, policy interpretation, and improvement of academic processes. Coordinate substantive-change screening, tracking, and required institutional notifications in consultation with responsible university officials. Lead Process Improvement and Cross-Functional Coordination: Evaluate academic governance workflows and recommend changes that improve clarity, timeliness, consistency, accountability, and stakeholder experience. Coordinate cross-functional implementation with academic units and offices responsible for curriculum, catalog, records, reporting, accreditation, and system or state approvals. Participate in departmental planning and special projects related to academic planning, program review, degree pathways, accreditation, and institutional effectiveness. Maintain professional knowledge of academic governance, regulatory expectations, accreditation requirements, and effective practices in higher education administration. Oversee the Office of the Associate Provost for Academic Strategy and Institutional Effectiveness. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Bachelor\u2019s degree. 2. A total of one (1) year (12 months) in education, training and/or work experience in the area of specialization inherent to the position. (Note: Master\u2019s Degree in an area consistent with the duties of the position may be substituted for one (1) year of work experience.) 3. Additional education, training, and/or work experience in the area of specialization (see specialty factors below). Specialty Factors: A total of two (2) years (24 months) work experience in administration (responsibility for day-to-day operation/oversight/coordination of a unit / program / system / process / function). One (1) additional year (12 months) of work experience supporting one or more high-level administrators and/or units in a complex organization, such as education or government. An additional year (12 months) of work experience using electronic tracking, reporting, or transaction process systems. Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in Higher Education, Public Administration, Business Administration, Educational Leadership, or a related field. Experience with academic governance policies, processes, and procedures in higher education. Experience managing academic catalogs or curricular approval processes. Experience working in higher education administration, academic affairs, accreditation, or related functions. Experience coordinating projects involving multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and complex timelines. Experience developing reports, maintaining records, and utilizing workflow, tracking, or project management systems. Experience interpreting policies, procedures, and regulatory requirements and communicating them to diverse audiences. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications, including Word and Excel, and the ability to learn new software systems and reporting tools. Knowledge of shared governance principles and academic decision-making structures in higher education. Knowledge of academic program and curriculum approval processes, accreditation, or regulatory compliance. Ability to interpret complex policies and translate them into clear operational guidance, workflows, and documentation requirements. Ability to coordinate multiple interdependent processes, stakeholders, deadlines, and approval authorities with a high degree of independent judgment. Ability to analyze records and requirements, identify discrepancies or risk, and recommend appropriate resolution. Ability to develop procedures, training materials, templates, status reports, and management information Strong written, oral, consultative, and cross-functional communication skills. Ability to represent the UIS professionally with university, system, state, accrediting, and other external stakeholders. Employment Policies and other information: Failure to accurately describe work experience, or failure to submit college transcripts may result in an applicant not being admitted to the exam. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1270?c=uis": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Public Management and Policy (MPP/MPA)", "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant Professor, Public Management and Policy (MPP/MPA) Springfield, IL, United States | 1005050 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/9/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor, Public Management and Policy (MPP/MPA) | Job Details Assistant Professor, Public Management and Policy (MPP/MPA) Posting Category: Summary: The School of Public Management & Policy is seeking an Assistant Professor to support our MPA/MPP programs beginning August 16, 2027. Required qualifications for the position include a doctorate in public policy, public administration, political science, or a related field. Teaching responsibilities include 3 courses per semester in the MPA program and/or MPP, and BPNA programs. Preference will be given to applicants who can offer graduate courses such as data science, statistics, economics, and community planning and economic development. Salary is competitive and dependent on qualifications. Experience in online teaching is desirable. This is a full-time on-campus tenure-track academic appointment. UIS tenure-system faculty are expected to be available and engaged in the campus community, with assigned professional responsibilities for teaching, scholarship, and service. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching: Courses to be taught include, but are not limited to - PAD 507 Information for Decision Making, a required core course for the MPA program, an elective course for the MPP&DPA programs; PAD 508 Economics and Public Policy, a required core course for the MPP program, and elective course for the MPA&DPA programs; PAD 526 Advanced Analytical Tools: Forecasting, Time Series Analysis, and Predictive Analytics, an elective course for the MPA, MPP&DPA programs; and PAD 554 Community Planning Tools, a required Community Planning graduate certificate course. Scholarship : Demonstrate a record of effective performance and accomplishment, according to the criteria for scholarship provided for in Article 3 of the UIS Faculty Personnel Policy. Service : Demonstrate a record of effective performance and accomplishment, according to the criteria for service provided for in Article 3 of the UIS Faculty Personnel Policy. Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in public policy, public administration, political science, or a related field Ability and willingness to teach graduate courses in various areas of public management and policy Evidence of teaching effectiveness Evidence of scholarship productivity Experience and/or willingness to teach in an online degree program A commitment to addressing inclusion in the classroom and preparing students to address inclusion in the workforce and community Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to applicants who can offer graduate courses such as data science, statistics, economics, and community planning and economic development. Application deadline: 10/19/2026 Nine-month salary: $64-66,000 Application instructions: Click the \"Apply Now\" button at the top or bottom of the posting, create or update your profile, complete the \nonline application, and upload current curriculum vita or resume, one publication sample, and student course evaluation results from at least two courses. Contact information for professional references will be requested later in the search process. Formal review \nof applications will begin soon after application deadline and continue until the position is filled or the search is terminated. About\nUIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves approximately 4,000 students in 60 undergraduate \nprograms of study, 41 minors, 44 graduate programs of study, 1 doctorate, 43 graduate certificates, coursework that leads to 8 ISBE endorsements. The academic curriculum offers students a strong liberal \narts core, a wide range of professional programs, and close faculty interaction. Making the most of its location in the state capital, UIS is broadly engaged in public policy and service. Its diverse \nstudent body includes traditional, non-traditional, and international students. Twenty-five percent of majors are in 17 undergraduate and graduate online degree programs and the campus has received \nseveral national awards for its implementation of online learning. UIS faculty are committed teachers, active scholars, and professionals in service to society. The University emphasizes excellence in \nteaching, and faculty are also expected to provide a balance of scholarship and service activities to meet requirements for tenure and promotion. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at https://www.uis.edu and the department/school web page at https://www.uis.edu/spmp About Springfield, Illinois: https://www.uis.edu/academic-affairs/about-our-springfield-community/ Union Affiliation: Tenure-track faculty positions at more than half-time are represented by the University Professionals of Illinois (UPI) Local 4100, University of Illinois Springfield United Faculty Chapter, IFT-AFT, AFL-CIO. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . The University of Illinois offers a very competitive benefits portfolio. Click for a complete list of Employee Benefits. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State Universities Retirement System You do not pay Social Security taxes and your earnings will not be on your Social Security record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages.) Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1288?c=uis": {"title": "Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (up to 3 positions)", "description": "Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (up to 3 positions) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (up to 3 positions) Springfield, IL, United States | 1005089 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/3/2026 Back to Search Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (up to 3 positions) Posting Category: The University of Illinois Springfield invites applications for three inaugural faculty positions (preferred start date January 1, 2027; latest start August 16, 2027) in Engineering Technology to launch the Bachelor of Applied Science in Engineering Technology (BAS-ET), beginning Fall 2027. These positions will form the founding faculty cohort and will collectively deliver the core curriculum, establish the work-based learning sequence with regional employers, and prepare for ABET ETAC accreditation. We are seeking candidates whose expertise spans applied engineering technology. The final composition of the cohort will be shaped by the strength of the applicant pool, with the goal of assembling a team that collectively covers the program's instructional needs. Preferred areas of expertise include automation, robotics, and industrial controls; engineering design, CAD/CAM, and manufacturing systems; systems integration, project management, and applied engineering practice; materials, measurement, and quality systems; and work-based learning coordination and industry partnership development. Significant industry experience is strongly preferred. A mix of tenure-track and non-tenure track hires is anticipated. View the tenure-track job posting at: https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1287?c=uis These are full-time on-campus and benefit-eligible non-tenured academic appointments. UIS faculty are expected to be available and engaged in the university community to perform professional responsibilities as assigned. Responsibilities: Teaching: Faculty will deliver core coursework in the Bachelor of Applied Science in Engineering Technology. Teaching assignments will be determined based on each faculty member's expertise and the collective needs of the founding cohort . Service: All faculty are expected to contribute to the development and growth of the BAS-ET program and the School of Applied Engineering through active participation in program-level, college-level, and university service. Service responsibilities include participation in the program's industry advisory board, including development and maintenance of employer relationships for work-based learning placements; community college partnership development, including articulation agreement planning and transfer pathway coordination; ABET ETAC accreditation preparation, self-study documentation, and continuous improvement processes; K-12 pipeline engagement, including support for the techX dual-credit program at the Capital Area Career Center; student recruitment activities, including prospective student outreach, campus visit participation, and community college advising events; and standard college and university committee service as assigned. In the program's early years, service will be weighted toward accreditation preparation and partnership development. As the program matures, faculty service responsibilities will normalize to reflect the standard expectations across the college.college and university committee service as assigned. Visa sponsorship is not available for these positions Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in engineering, engineering technology, engineering education, manufacturing, applied science, or a closely related STEM discipline Minimum five years of substantial professional industry experience in an engineering or technical leadership role Demonstrated ability or potential to teach in applied, hands-on, lab-intensive learning environments Commitment to work-based learning and employer-integrated education Preferred Qualifications : Experience with ABET-accredited programs or accreditation processes\nExperience with community college transfer student populations\nExperience designing or coordinating cooperative education, internship, or work-based learning programs\nExpertise in one or more: automation, robotics, and industrial controls; engineering design, CAD/CAM, and manufacturing systems; systems integration and project management; materials, measurement, and quality systems Application deadline (5pm): 10/19/2026 Nine-month salary: $110-130,000 Application instructions: Click the \"Apply Now\" button, create or update your profile, complete the online application, and upload 1) cover letter addressing the required and preferred qualifications, including which of the program's instructional areas the candidate is prepared to teach and your interest in a founding-faculty role, 2) curriculum vitae or resume, including professional industry experience,  3) statement of teaching philosophy, addressing applied, hands-on, lab-intensive instruction and experience with student populations such as transfer students and working adults, and 4) a statement of professional practice. Contact information for professional references will be requested later in the search process. Formal review of applications will begin soon after the application deadline and continue until the position is filled or the search is terminated. About UIS: Located in the state \ncapital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members \nof the University of Illinois system. The University serves \napproximately 4,000 students in 60 undergraduate programs of study, 41 \nminors, 44 graduate programs of study, 1 doctorate, 43 graduate \ncertificates, and coursework that leads to 8 ISBE endorsements. The \nacademic curriculum offers students a strong liberal arts core, a wide \nrange of professional programs, and close faculty interaction. Making \nthe most of its location in the state capital, UIS is broadly engaged in\n public policy and service. Its diverse student body includes \ntraditional, non-traditional, and international students. Twenty-five \npercent of majors are in 17 undergraduate and graduate online degree \nprograms and the campus has received several national awards for its \nimplementation of online learning. UIS faculty are committed teachers, \nactive scholars, and professionals in service to society. The University\n emphasizes excellence in teaching, and faculty are also expected to \nprovide a balance of scholarship and service activities to meet \nrequirements for tenure and promotion. You are encouraged to visit the \nuniversity web page at\u00a0https://www.uis.edu and the college web page at https://www.uis.edu/chst. About Springfield, Illinois: https://www.uis.edu/academic-affairs/about-our-springfield-community Union Affiliation: This position is included in a bargaining unit (UPI Local 4100 UIS Nontenure-Track Faculty Union). This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1287?c=uis": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (3 positions)", "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (3 positions) Springfield, IL, United States | 1005088 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/3/2026 Back to Search Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (3 positions) | Job Details Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (3 positions) Posting Category: Summary: The University of Illinois Springfield invites applications for up to three inaugural tenure-track faculty positions (Assistant or Associate Professor, preferred start date January 1, 2027 and latest start date August 16, 2027) in Engineering Technology to launch the Bachelor of Applied Science in Engineering Technology (BAS-ET), beginning Fall 2027. These positions will form the founding faculty cohort and will collectively deliver the core curriculum, establish the work-based learning sequence with regional employers, and prepare for ABET ETAC accreditation. We are seeking candidates whose expertise spans applied engineering technology. The final composition of the cohort will be shaped by the strength of the applicant pool, with the goal of assembling a team that collectively covers the program's instructional needs. Preferred areas of expertise include automation, robotics, and industrial controls; engineering design, CAD/CAM, and manufacturing systems; systems integration, project management, and applied engineering practice; materials, measurement, and quality systems; and work-based learning coordination and industry partnership development. Significant industry experience is strongly preferred. These are full-time on-campus tenure-track academic appointments. UIS tenure-system faculty are expected to be available and engaged in the university community, with assigned professional responsibilities for teaching, scholarship, and service. A mix of tenure-system and non-tenure system faculty may comprise this cohort. View the clinical faculty posting:\u00a0https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1288?c=uis Visa sponsorship is not available for these positions. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching: Faculty will deliver core coursework in the Bachelor of Applied Science in Engineering Technology. Teaching assignments will be determined based on each faculty member's expertise and the collective needs of the founding cohort. Scholarship: Faculty are expected to develop an active program of applied research or scholarly activity appropriate to the discipline of engineering technology. This may include industry-sponsored applied research projects with regional partners; design, development, and evaluation of work-based learning pedagogy and assessment models; scholarship of teaching and learning in engineering technology education; workforce development research in collaboration with employer and community college partners; and contributions to professional societies such as ASEE or ABET. Given the applied nature of the program, scholarship that bridges academic inquiry and industry practice is especially valued. The expectation is that scholarly activity will be productive and sustained, consistent with the standards for tenure and promotion at UIS, while recognizing that the early years of a new program will require significant effort in curriculum development, accreditation preparation, and partnership building. Service: All faculty are expected to contribute to the development and growth of the BAS-ET program and the School of Applied Engineering through active participation in program-level, college-level, and university service. Service responsibilities include participation in the program's industry advisory board, including development and maintenance of employer relationships for work-based learning placements; community college partnership development, including articulation agreement planning and transfer pathway coordination; ABET ETAC accreditation preparation, self-study documentation, and continuous improvement processes; K-12 pipeline engagement, including support for the techX dual-credit program at the Capital Area Career Center; student recruitment activities, including prospective student outreach, campus visit participation, and community college advising events; and standard college and university committee service as assigned. In the program's early years, service will be weighted toward accreditation preparation and partnership development. As the program matures, faculty service responsibilities will normalize to reflect the standard expectations across the college.college and university committee service as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree in engineering, engineering technology, engineering education, manufacturing, applied science, or a closely related STEM discipline (ABD considered with expected completion within one year of start date) Professional experience in an engineering, manufacturing, automation, construction, infrastructure, or related technical industry Demonstrated ability or potential to teach in applied, hands-on, lab-intensive learning environments Record of or clear potential for applied research, scholarship, or creative activity appropriate to rank Commitment to work-based learning and employer-integrated education Preferred Qualifications: Experience with ABET-accredited programs or accreditation processes Experience with community college transfer student populations Experience designing or coordinating cooperative education, internship, or work-based learning programs Record of industry-sponsored projects, applied research, or scholarship of teaching and learning Expertise in one or more: automation, robotics, and industrial controls; engineering design, CAD/CAM, and manufacturing systems; systems integration and project management; materials, measurement, and quality systems Application deadline: 10/19/2026 Nine-month salary: $110-130,000 Application instructions: Click the \"Apply Now\" button at the top or bottom of the posting, create or update your profile, complete the \nonline application, and upload 1) cover letter addressing\n     the required and preferred qualifications, including which of the\n     program's instructional areas the candidate is prepared to teach and their\n     interest in a founding-faculty role, 2) curriculum vitae or\n     resume, including professional industry experience, 3) statement of teaching philosophy, addressing applied, hands-on, lab-intensive instruction and experience with student populations such as transfer students and working adults, 4) statement of applied research/scholarship interests, and 5) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire).\n. Contact information for professional references will be requested later in the search process. Formal review \nof applications will begin soon after application deadline and continue until the position is filled or the search is terminated. About\nUIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves approximately 4,000 students in 60 undergraduate \nprograms of study, 41 minors, 44 graduate programs of study, 1 doctorate, 43 graduate certificates, coursework that leads to 8 ISBE endorsements. The academic curriculum offers students a strong liberal \narts core, a wide range of professional programs, and close faculty interaction. Making the most of its location in the state capital, UIS is broadly engaged in public policy and service. Its diverse \nstudent body includes traditional, non-traditional, and international students. Twenty-five percent of majors are in 17 undergraduate and graduate online degree programs and the campus has received \nseveral national awards for its implementation of online learning. UIS faculty are committed teachers, active scholars, and professionals in service to society. The University emphasizes excellence in \nteaching, and faculty are also expected to provide a balance of scholarship and service activities to meet requirements for tenure and promotion. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at https://www.uis.edu and the college web page at: https://www.uis.edu/chst About Springfield, Illinois: https://www.uis.edu/academic-affairs/about-our-springfield-community/ Union Affiliation: Tenure-track faculty positions at more than half-time are represented by the University Professionals of Illinois (UPI) Local 4100, University of Illinois Springfield United Faculty Chapter, IFT-AFT, AFL-CIO. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . The University of Illinois offers a very competitive benefits portfolio. Click for a complete list of Employee Benefits. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State Universities Retirement System You do not pay Social Security taxes and your earnings will not be on your Social Security record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages.) Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/868?c=uis": {"title": "Extra Help Event Attendant - 50 Vacancies", "description": "Extra Help Event Attendant - 50 Vacancies | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Extra Help Event Attendant - 50 Vacancies Springfield, IL, United States | 1004083 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 5/27/2026 Back to Search Extra Help Event Attendant - 50 Vacancies Posting Category: About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: Open Until Filled Hourly Rate: $20.00 Summary: Extra Help Event Attendants provide event related services in a variety of different areas of operations including: concession stand, merchandise sales, artist runner and access control. Duties & Responsibilities: Parking Attendant (Non-Driving): Assist in setting up traffic cones and signs for event parking and VIP parking. Provide general patron assistance and directions into the building and to events. Monitor parking lot for available parking spaces. Assist in tearing down traffic cones and signs at the end of the shift. Provide patron assistance exiting the building, to cars, and exiting the University. Concession Stand Attendant (Non-Alcohol): Serve as the primary point of contact for customer service and sales at events. Prepare the concession stand for sales, ensuring all areas are clean and stocked. Operate point of sale systems, cash drawers, and credit card machines. Take orders for beverages and food items, finalize sales, and restock products. Shut down and reconcile point of sale systems and cash drawers. Clean all machines, countertops, and other work areas. Ensure the concession stand is ready for the next use. Merchandise Seller: Act as the PAS representative in fulfilling artist merchandise sales. Work with artist\u2019s representative to prepare and sell merchandise. Operate point of sale systems, cash drawers, and credit card machines. Assist with finalizing product counts and shutting down merchandise areas. Clean all work areas. Artist Attendant (Non-Driving): Assist in fulfilling the needs of the artists and their traveling staff. Prepare and monitor hospitality rooms, stock supplies, and clean hospitality areas. Monitor access control at backstage doors and other specified areas. Artist Runner/Attendant (Driving): Fulfill all duties of the Artist Attendant role. Run errands and fulfill hospitality contracts. Drive members of the artist\u2019s team locally (vehicle provided by the university). Access Control Attendant: Ensure patrons, artists, and staff follow policies and procedures for accessing event areas. Place signage and access control features, scan tickets, review credentials, and inspect packages. Guide patrons through metal detectors and request UIS Police assistance if necessary. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma, some college preferred. Age requirement: 18 years old minimum for all positions OR 21 years old for driving positions as indicated above. UIS background check \u2013 must pass prior to starting work. AED (Automated External Defibrillator) training (provided). Cash handling and credit card training for applicable positions (provided). Applicants must be able to provide exceptional customer service to diverse groups of people including: the public, students, event promoters, and University department representatives. Must have a positive friendly attitude, be clean and well-groomed, possess good interpersonal communication skills, and remain calm while managing a life safety evacuation or other emergency. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Standing for long periods of time. Occasional lifting, up to 30 lbs. Physical Demands: Standing : Frequently Walking : Frequently Sitting : Rarely Lifting : Frequently Carrying : Frequently Pushing : Frequently Pulling : Frequently Climbing : Rarely Balancing : Rarely Stooping : Occasionally Kneeling : Occasionally Crouching : Occasionally Crawling : Rarely Reaching : Occasionally Handling : Frequently Grasping : Frequently Feeling : Occasionally Talking : Frequently Hearing : Frequently Repetitive Motions : Frequently Eye/Hand/Foot Coordination : Frequently Taste/Smell : Rarely Performing Manual Tasks : Frequently Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence,\nequity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic\ninformation, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility This position is not eligible for benefits. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State Universities Retirement System You do not pay Social Security taxes and your earnings will not be on your Social Security record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages.) Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1084?c=uis": {"title": "Adjunct (Per Course) Teaching Opportunities", "description": "Adjunct (Per Course) Teaching Opportunities | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Adjunct (Per Course) Teaching Opportunities Springfield, IL, United States | req1084 Share Save Job Posted on: 9/18/2025 Back to Search Adjunct (Per Course) Teaching Opportunities Posting Category:\u00a0Hide Apply Now The University of Illinois Springfield has occasional need for individuals to teach on a per-course, or \u201cadjunct\u201d basis. Qualified individuals are welcome to apply to the specific adjunct posting for one or more departments/schools on the Adjunct Job Board at https://go.uis.edu/adjunct-jobs . A unit may contact an applicant when a need for someone with their qualifications and experience arises. View Adjunct FAQ:\u00a0https://www.uis.edu/academic-affairs/faculty-resources/adjunct-opportunities Important note: In order to maintain employment eligibility, adjunct faculty are required to complete mandatory annual employee training, including (but not limited to) Ethics, and Preventing Harassment & Discrimination.\u00a0Adjunct faculty teaching online courses must successfully complete the Building Digital Community (BDC) self-paced course during their first semester teaching online to be eligible to teach additional online courses at UIS. BDC is offered free of charge through the Center for Online Learning, Research and Service (COLRS). Email COLRS (colrs@uis.edu) to enroll in BDC. Application Instructions: Link to job postings for programs that occasionally have a need for adjunct \"per course\" instructors: https://go.uis.edu/adjunct-jobs About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves approximately 4,000 students in 60 undergraduate programs of\nstudy, 41 minors, 44 graduate programs of study, 1 doctorate, 43 graduate\ncertificates, coursework that leads to 8 ISBE endorsements. The academic curriculum offers students a strong liberal arts core, a wide range of\nprofessional programs, and close faculty interaction. Making the most of its location in the state capital, UIS is broadly engaged in public policy and service. Its diverse student body includes traditional, non-traditional, and international students. Twenty-five percent of majors are in 17 undergraduate and graduate online degree programs and the campus has received several national awards for its implementation of online learning. UIS faculty are committed teachers, active scholars, and professionals in service to society. The University emphasizes excellence in teaching, and faculty are also expected to provide a balance of scholarship and service activities to meet requirements for tenure and promotion. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at https://www.uis.edu This position is not eligible for benefits. About Springfield, Illinois: https://www.uis.edu/academic-affairs/about-our-springfield-community Adjunct employment FAQ: https://go.uis.edu/adjunct-faq The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/869?c=uis": {"title": "Extra Help Stagehand - 50 vacancies", "description": "Extra Help Stagehand - 50 vacancies | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Extra Help Stagehand - 50 vacancies Springfield, IL, United States | 1004085 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/6/2024 Back to Search Extra Help Stagehand - 50 vacancies Posting Category: About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: Open Until Filled Hourly Rate: $20.07 per hour Summary: Under direct supervision from the supervisor - responsible for the coordination of necessary work, to perform all necessary work required for the preparation, operation and removal of various event equipment; for the operation of stage lighting equipment; for the operation and maintenance of the counter-balanced fly system and associated pin-rail and pick-line rigging; for the operation and maintenance of sound and lighting systems; for the set-up and moving of temporary show equipment brought to the operating unit; for the installation and removal of theatrical scenery and house curtains within the venues; and for the maintenance, laundry, and repair of costumes, towels and other fabric items including acting as dresser for actors. The work of the rigger specifically does NOT include operation of the counter-balanced fly system, sand-bag/hemp pin-rail system, or simple pick-lines raising items such as cable bundles off of the floor to allow for safe passage underneath by crew and performers.\nThis position will perform all the below duties and responsibilities while maintaining a safe work environment at all times and performing work in a safe manner at all-time including wearing/utilizing all Personal Protection Equipment (PPE) as required by employer. Duties & Responsibilities: Attendance (paid) at employer-required safety training sessions Load & unload theatrical equipment into and out of vehicles as required including stacking and unstacking of equipment Move theatrical equipment into and out of venue storage areas Perform all work required to operate and maintain the safety, trim, balance, and proper rigging of the counterbalanced fly system and associated winched cables, pin-rail equipment and pick-lines Perform such technical specialties as the splicing of cables and ropes, the use of stage weights and braces, the\nmaintenance and correct use of tie lines and pick lines, the maintenance and repair of curtains, and the periodic inspection of curtains in storage to prevent damage. Operate mechanical systems such as pit-lifts, orchestra shell winches, chain motors, etc. Operating of chain motors does NOT also include functions performed by EXTRA HELP RIGGERS. Operate personnel-lift devices Hang, connect to the dimming system, lamp, focus and color theatrical lighting instruments for general and specific uses Move and place audio gear such as microphones, speakers, monitors, control boards and cable as required Install, remove, operate and reconfigure stage curtains, portable flooring, scenery, props and other theatrical items as required. Sweeping and mopping of stage area as required for safety and proper audience presentation Maintain, move, set up and operate spotlights as required Maintain and operate lighting and audio control systems Install, maintain and operate as needed equipment hung from counter-weighted battens. Setup, maintain (including laundry), repair and place back into storage costumes, wigs and other items worn by\nperformers including towels and associated fabric items. Also assist performers with putting on and taking off costume items. Perform other duties commonly associated with stage operations as required Minimum Qualifications: Basic entry-level knowledge of a back-stage theatrical working environment including terminology & standard operating procedures usually acquired through formal education in the performing arts field or previous volunteer/work experience as a stage crew member in a high school, college, community theatre, music club, regional theatre, or professional performance venue. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Normal ability to hear, see, speak, smell in a backstage environment which at times can be darkened, crowed, and noisy with multiple hazards Ability to move quickly unaided Ability to climb stairs, ladders and work at heights. Ability to lift and move heavy objects Ability to follow detailed or general directions on how to perform tasks. Ability to work varying and unusual work schedules Ability to follow and comply with employer's safety rules and regulations Physical Demands: Standing : Frequently Walking : Frequently Sitting : Rarely Lifting : Frequently Carrying : Frequently Pushing : Frequently Pulling : Frequently Climbing : Occasionally Balancing : Occasionally Stooping : Occasionally Kneeling : Occasionally Crouching : Occasionally Crawling : Occasionally Reaching : Occasionally Handling : Frequently Grasping : Occasionally Feeling : Occasionally Talking : Frequently Hearing : Frequently Repetitive Motions : Frequently Eye/Hand/Foot Coordination : Frequently Taste/Smell : Rarely Performing Manual Tasks : Frequently Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence,\nequity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic\ninformation, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility This position is not eligible for benefits. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State Universities Retirement System You do not pay Social Security taxes and your earnings will not be on your Social Security record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages.) Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/840?c=uis": {"title": "ION Instructor (per course)", "description": "ION Instructor (per course) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) ION Instructor (per course) Springfield, IL, United States | req840 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/6/2024 Back to Search ION Instructor (per course) Posting Category: The University\nof Illinois Springfield ION professional eLearning program (ION) routinely\nseeks competent, qualified professionals to teach on a per-course basis based\non course offerings and need. ION often seeks\ncontent experts to develop and deliver specialized training programs to\nbusinesses and community partners. ION offers non-credit courses, workshops\nand professional training programs. ION\u00a0 programs feature 4- or\n8-week asynchronous instructor-led courses. Read more about the\u00a0ION eLeanring Program at www.uis.edu/ion. Responsibilities: Teach ION professional eLearning courses by defining clear learning\nobjectives and understanding your audience's needs. Organize content into\nstructured modules, with practical applications like case studies and projects.\nUse an LMS (Moodle) to engage participants through discussion forums, and\nregular assignments with feedback. Ensure accessibility and continuously\nimproving the course by analyzing participation data and feedback, updating\ncontent regularly, and staying informed on best practices in online teaching\nand the subject taught. Minimum Qualifications: Required: Previous\n     experience teaching in a hybrid and/or fully online classroom at the\n     collegiate level is required for ALL ION classes. Experience\n     leveraging educational technology tools and learning management systems is\n     required for all ION Technology courses. All CAPE faculty must be subject\n     matter experts in the\u00a0field\u00a0for which they will be hired. Demonstrated experience in\n     teaching (minimum of 3 years) and/or administering (minimum of 2 years) in\n     online programs in a higher education setting. Must\n     be a subject matter expert in the area for which you are applying. Demonstrated\n     ability to deliver content that is student-centered and actively engages\n     students with diverse interests and needs. Knowledge\n     of career, professional development, experiential learning, workplace\n     trends, and/or service-learning best practices. Preferred: Master's degree Additional certifications/credentials held in the area for which you are applying. Application deadline: Open Application instructions: Click the \"Apply Now\" button, create or update\u00a0your profile, \ncomplete the\nonline application, and upload a cover letter addressing the \nresponsibilities of the position, current curriculum vita or resume, and unofficial transcripts. Contact information for professional references may be requested. About UIS: Located in the state \ncapital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members \nof the University of Illinois system. The University serves \napproximately 4,000 students in 60 undergraduate programs of study, 41 \nminors, 44 graduate programs of study, 1 doctorate, 43 graduate \ncertificates, coursework that leads to 8 ISBE endorsements. The academic\n curriculum offers students a strong liberal arts core, a wide range of \nprofessional programs, and close faculty interaction. Making the most of\n its location in the state capital, UIS is broadly engaged in public \npolicy and service. Its diverse student body includes traditional, \nnon-traditional, and international students. Twenty-five percent of \nmajors are in 17 undergraduate and graduate online degree programs and \nthe campus has received several national awards for its implementation \nof online learning. UIS faculty are committed teachers, active scholars,\n and professionals in service to society. The University emphasizes \nexcellence in teaching, and faculty are also expected to provide a \nbalance of scholarship and service activities to meet requirements for \ntenure and promotion. You are encouraged to visit the University web \npage at www.uis.edu. This position is not eligible for benefits. About Springfield, Illinois: https://www.uis.edu/academic-affairs/about-our-springfield-community Adjunct employment FAQ: https://go.uis.edu/adjunct-faq The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1338?c=uis": {"title": "Program Coordinator - Disability Specialist", "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Program Coordinator - Disability Specialist Springfield, IL, United States | 1005150 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/13/2026 Back to Search Program Coordinator - Disability Specialist | Job Details Program Coordinator - Disability Specialist Posting Category: About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: 11/6/2026 Minimum Starting Salary: $23.03 per hour/7.5 hour day Summary: Ensure students with disabilities receive the appropriate academic accommodations for exams in our Testing Center. Coordinate  the Testing Center by ensuring rules and regulations are followed; students are given their correct accommodations; professors  are instructed on the Testing Center rules. Make sure the exam schedule is updated daily and contact professors or students  regarding changes in exams. Assist with intake and review and approve students' documentation for services. Assist the director as a liaison to the campus and university units to uphold policies and procedures. Duties & Responsibilities: Coordinates daily operations of the ODS Testing Center; works closely with students, staff, and faculty to implement goals and objectives of the ODS Testing Center; resolves conflicts and ensures efficient operation of the ODS Testing Center. Maintain the spreadsheet of all the exams for the Testing Center Provide students using accommodated testing with assistance or student employees to assist them. Provide initial intake for new students that need ODS services. Meet with new and registered students to review and approve their documentation. Prepare and issue academic accommodation letters to students. Collaborate with both the student and professors to ensure the requested academic accommodations are being provided with exemplary services. Collaborate with staff on the production of alternate text format and alternate test scheduling. Assist with testing duties such as proctoring exams, scribing or reading exams. Follow up with registered students and professors to ensure that academic accommodations are being carried out throughout the academic semester. Listen and address any student concerns that may arise throughout the semester in regard to their academic accommodation in the classroom. Collaborate with the director to compile and analyze data and statistics pertinent to the Office of Disability Services. Ensure ADA compliance and best practices are followed. Act as a liaison to campus and university units and represent the ODS office at internal and external events including orientations, open houses, presentations, and graduation. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Bachelor\u2019s degree. 2. A total of one (1) year (12 months) in education, training and/or work experience in the area of specialization inherent to the position. (Note: Master\u2019s Degree in an area consistent with the duties of the position may be substituted for one (1) year of work experience.) 3. Based on position requirements, additional education, training, and/or work experience in the area of specialization inherent to the position, may be required. Additional education, training and/or work experience in the area of specialization: Preferred Qualifications: -1 year of experience working with Excel data base scheduling; experience in Managing an office and student employees - Minimum of 7 years of experience involving position of increasing responsibility including at least 2 of direct experience working with students with disabilities and a detailed knowledge of the Americans with Disability Act and Section 504 relating to accommodation for college and university students. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Skill in oral and written communication Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and handle stressful situations/people Employment Policies and other information: Failure to accurately describe work experience, or failure to submit college transcripts may result in an applicant not being admitted to the exam. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1337?c=uis": {"title": "Financial Aid Coordinator", "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Financial Aid Coordinator Springfield, IL, United States | 1005208 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/7/2026 Back to Search Financial Aid Coordinator | Job Details Financial Aid Coordinator Posting Category: About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: 10/21/2026 Minimum Starting Salary: $24.85 per hour / 7.5 hour work day Summary: The Financial Aid Coordinator advises undergraduate students and participates in all functions and processing of Federal, State and Institutional financial aid programs. The coordinator provides customer service and counseling to financial aid applicants and families via phone, email, in person and virtual visits. Duties & Responsibilities: Serves as an undergraduate advisor managing the counseling and advising of undergraduate students regarding financial aid programs, availability and eligibility.  Review and award undergraduate financial aid applicants in accordance with federal, state and institutional regulations and policies: Performs data-entry and tracks financial aid awards on the Banner System;  Meets with parents and students virtually, in-person and via phone. Administers Athletic aid including awarding, tracking, working with Athletics Compliance, processing renewals, certifications, and cancellations, performing data entry into NCAA Compliance Assistant, and answering student-athlete and coaches\u2019 questions. Processes and monitors all verification documents as well as other required documentation to complete aid eligibility. Packages summer aid, satisfies tracking requirements, resolves financial aid holds, communicates difficult situations to students and parents, and conducts additional student follow-up as needed. Administers the Teacher Education programs including awarding, certifying, communicating with students and the School of Education faculty, and resolving issues. Edits the financial aid website, creates and updates forms, and revises other materials in compliance with digital accessibility and ensures required financial aid consumer information meets financial aid compliance regulations. Resolves over-awards and adjusts budgets accordingly; ensures funds are reduced or returned as needed and processes Student Account Payment Requests Participate in events and presentations for current and prospective students, such as new student orientations and open houses. Participate in training and professional development opportunities and represent the financial aid office on various groups or committees across campus, as delegated. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Any one or combination totaling three (3) years (36 months) from the categories below: A. College coursework in any discipline, as measured by the following conversion table or its proportional equivalent:\n    i. 30 semester hours equals one (1) year (12 months)\n    ii. Associate\u2019s Degree (60 semester hours) equals eighteen months (18 months)\n    iii. 90 semester hours equals two (2) years (24 months)\n    iv. Bachelor\u2019s Degree (120 semester hours) equals three (3) years (36 months) B. Work experience coordinating office, business, or customer service/relations activities. 2. One (1) year (12 months) of higher education, student services, or closely related experience. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Banner student financial aid software Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of all federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid regulations as they apply to packaging and disbursement of financial aid, disbursement of refunds, and Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP). Knowledge of the student application process. Knowledge of Microsoft Office \u2013 Outlook, Excel, and Word and other computer programs. Skill in customer service, and oral and written communication. Skill in time management, organizing work assignments, and responding quickly and effectively to challenges. Ability to interpret and apply internal and government policies, procedures and regulations. Ability to work in an environment that can be fast-paced and stressful. Travel Requirements: 5% Professional Development Travel Employment Policies and other information: Failure to accurately describe work experience, or failure to submit college transcripts may result in an applicant not being admitted to the exam. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1322?c=uis": {"title": "Manager and Sponsorship Account Executive", "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Manager and Sponsorship Account Executive Springfield, IL, United States | 1005128 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/21/2026 Back to Search Manager and Sponsorship Account Executive | Job Details Manager and Sponsorship Account Executive Posting Category:\u00a0E About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs.  You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: 10/16/2026 Minimum Starting Salary: $70,000 + bonus structure Summary: The Manager and Sponsorship Account Executive is responsible NPR Illinois' budget and funding portfolio, acting as NPR's revenue strategist and manager. The MSAE will be the primary executive securing funding from businesses, foundations, and individuals to support the public journalism of NPR Illinois and the Illinois Public Radio Network through sponsorships and acknowledgments in digital, broadcast, and print media. This position engages with area businesses for the purpose of securing sponsorship and advertisement revenue. The position will also oversee all annual giving and non-gift business revenue. Duties & Responsibilities: Develop sponsorship business gifts and revenue, requiring identifying prospects, securing meetings, doing client needs analysis, responding with off-the-shelf or custom proposals (asks). Manage sponsorship execution, closing orders, entering, writing, and producing announcements, securing digital creative, entering digital orders, billing, stewardship, and renewal. If revenue results allow the addition of another sponsorship account executive in the future, this position will supervise it. Build and maintain strong relationships with current business supporters. Anticipate, meet and/or exceed donor needs, wants, and expectations - customer service. Develop stewardship techniques to ensure renewals and added commitments. Supervise and coordinate overall fundraising and revenue activities and resources to maximize revenue, create a positive culture, and retain talent. Tracks all revenue KPIs to exceed goals. Goals need to exceed prior fiscal year results and include additional revenue to cover fundraising labor and expenses. Supervise the annual giving/marketing coordinator \u2018s community engagement efforts and promotional partnerships to grow audience and convert into financial supporters, and to create sponsorship opportunities. Support fundraising events, donor appreciation gatherings, and community engagement initiatives. Supervise the annual giving/marketing coordinator \u2018s promotion of NPR Illinois\u2019 relevant content, services, and events using digital and broadcast inventory, external advertising, and partnerships. Strong supervision of planning and tracking of digital marketing. Oversee digital and website updates related to membership, campaigns, and promotions. Coordinate with the Director of Development, Major Gifts, and UIS Office of Advancement to align goals, communicate on donors, and collect data for full reporting of all revenue for NPR Illinois. Support supervisor in executing other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Business Administration, or a related field 2. Minimum of three years sales experience Preferred Qualifications: 1. Master's degree in Marketing, Business Administration, or a related field 2. One (1) year of previous public radio underwriting experience Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Ability to communicate persuasively to groups and individuals Ability to organize, manage multiple assignments, and be self-directed in leading oneself, staff, and volunteers to actively solicit funds from businesses, nonprofits, foundations, and other prospects Possess a valid driver's license Punctuality Possess a developed writing style that results in effective acknowledgments (ads) Experience in using social/digital media to secure revenue Proficiency in computer skills, including word processing, spreadsheets, and proprietary account management software (WideOrbit/Blackbaud).  Ability to work with a variety of Windows-based software programs to create presentations. Ability to lift 25 pounds on occasion Attention to detail Ability to maintain confidentiality of donor files and information Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures, or government regulations Ability to write reports, business correspondence, and procedure manuals Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, clients, customers, and the general public Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form Knowledge of regional market including decision makers, events, and key accounts Ability to operate broadcast equipment with an emphasis on digital audio production Ability to apply basic concepts of algebra and work with spreadsheets and account for cash and trade according to GAP Physical Demands: Standing : Occasionally Walking : Occasionally Sitting : Frequently Lifting : Occasionally Talking : Frequently Hearing : Frequently Working Conditions: Noise : Occasionally Atmospheric Conditions : Occasionally Travel Requirements: 70% This position will require several hours a day traveling the region and attending meetings.  This position also requires daily time at the computer.  Other demands include climbing stairs, negotiating prevailing weather conditions while traveling, and periods of standing. Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1320?c=uis": {"title": "Executive Director, Innovation and Opportunity", "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Executive Director, Innovation and Opportunity Springfield, IL, United States | 1005151 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/1/2026 Back to Search Executive Director, Innovation and Opportunity | Job Details Executive Director, Innovation and Opportunity Posting Category:\u00a0E About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs.  You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: Open Until Filled Please apply by September 18, 2026 for priority consideration. Proposed Annual Salary: $120,000 Summary: The Executive Director of Innovation and Opportunity (ED) at the University of Illinois Springfield will lead innovation and economic development efforts at UIS to benefit the regional economy in collaboration with local industry, government partners, Continuing and Professional Education (CAPE), and the Illinois Innovation Network (IIN). These efforts will be primarily conducted through the development and execution of related programming at Innovate Springfield, UIS' downtown Springfield innovation center and founding hub of the IIN. The Executive Director (ED) will lead Innovate Springfield's strategic framework across five interconnected pillars: business incubation and venture growth; business modernization and applied innovation; CAPE-delivered professional education and workforce development; student talent pipeline and engagement; and emerging technology awareness. Working closely with UIS leaders, faculty, staff, students, and community partners, the ED will develop and implement entrepreneurial and applied innovation initiatives that advance these strategic priorities. These activities will accelerate regional technology adoption, foster interdisciplinary collaboration, strengthen educational opportunities, inform public policy, and promote social innovation throughout the region. Duties & Responsibilities: Innovate Springfield Strategy and Governance. Work with internal and external partners to resource, develop, direct and implement all Innovate Springfield strategies aligned with UIS\u2019 strategic priorities and the Innovate Springfield strategic framework, and ensure the successful execution of Innovate Springfield operations and UIS innovation and economic development activities in collaboration with other program leads. Staff and lead advisory boards and related committees, ensuring regional input is translated into UIS programs, partnerships and measurable outcomes. Lead all aspects of programming across Innovate Springfield\u2019s five pillars \u2014 business incubation and acceleration, business modernization and applied innovation, professional education and workforce development, student talent pipeline, and emerging-technology awareness. Financial Sustainability. Develop, lead and ensure financial support and viability of Innovate Springfield\u2019s operations, as well as the business incubation and acceleration programs and Innovate Springfields\u2019s partnership model with Continuing and Professional Education (CAPE) for scalable, credential-generating programming. Develop, implement, and manage Innovate Springfield's operations and budget to ensure efficient service delivery and long-term financial sustainability. Collaborate with UIS Advancement and program leaders to secure financial support for Innovate Springfield's operations and programs. Establish and monitor meaningful performance measures, including a quarterly outcomes dashboard, to evaluate progress and organizational success. Programming Effectiveness. Ensure effectiveness across all Innovate Springfield programs \u2014 including business modernization and applied innovation (such as a recurring AI-adoption demonstration series and the region\u2019s AI community of practice), CAPE-delivered professional education and stackable credentials, and emerging-technology awareness \u2014 by working with other UIS leaders responsible for programing in such areas as technology and research commercialization, social innovation, public policy, and experiential and workforce education, as well as other program areas determined by the UIS Chancellor. Regional Partnerships. Develop and coordinate all UIS\u2019 initiatives with other UIS leaders responsible for programing to bring innovation to bear on the broad range of community and regional needs and problems. Actively engage current and potential partners in business, finance, government, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing, philanthropy, and scientific communities, as well as academic partners across the IIN, to invest in and advance an entrepreneurial and technology-adoption culture within and beyond UIS to strengthen economic development and innovation in the Springfield region. Academic and Student Engagement. Work with academic units \u2014 including the College of Business and Management, the College of Health, Science and Technology, and CAPE \u2014 to develop high-impact, applied learning opportunities for students related to innovation, entrepreneurship, and business modernization, and to connect youth and workforce programming to UIS degree and certificate pathways, with relevance to local economic and community development. Serve as UIS representative on IIN Council and various UI System committees. Staff Supervision. Supervise and oversee Innovate Springfield staff, as well as participating business incubation and CAPE program partners, for Innovate Springfield programing and operational success. Provide effective leadership, direction and support for staff to be successful at their assigned duties. Give staff frequent performance feedback and support their professional development. Visibility and Reporting. Develop and implement strategies, including regular dashboard reporting to the Advisory Board and UIS leadership, to highlight the value and successes of UIS\u2019 innovative and economic development activities in order to enhance Innovate Springfield visibility and reputation with internal and external stakeholders, including UIS leaders, faculty, students, business leaders, public officials and IIN partners. Advisory Role. Advise the Chancellor on economic development, innovation, and emerging-technology issues, and participate in committees, working groups, etc., as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree from an accredited institution (in some cases, extensive work experience in innovation, incubation and/or economic development fields could replace a master\u2019s degree requirement; in such cases, a bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution is required) A strong track record of leading innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystems and programs, including experience at innovation centers and/or business incubators \u25cf\tStrong background in business commercialization, community and regional economic development, and social innovation \u25cf\tExperience and deep knowledge of the requisites of the business startup process, including business planning, operations, financing and insight into local economic and social conditions \u25cf\tSupervisory experience Preferred Qualifications: Advanced degree from an accredited institution Experience working with faculty, staff and senior academic leadership at a higher education institution Investment and commercialization expertise; ability to identify, evaluate and effectuate investments Technical skill in projecting the economic and social impact of new and developing businesses and initiatives Experience with business incubation and acceleration Experience with business modernization, applied AI, or data-driven technology-adoption programming Experience partnering with professional/continuing education units to convert applied programming into scalable credentials and workforce training Familiarity with emerging technologies (e.g., artificial intelligence, data analytics, cybersecurity) and their translation into accessible public programming Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Demonstrated passion for innovation in general and for bringing ideas to market Demonstrated success establishing and maintaining relationships across a variety of networks, such as in higher education, business sectors, venture investing, nonprofits, and/or community organizations Success leading large teams, administrating committees and supervising employees High level of integrity and exceptional interpersonal and team-building skills Excellent written and oral communication skills Cultural competency to work with diverse groups and build an inclusive work environment Willingness to accommodate meetings/activities outside normal business hours Passion for advancing communities through innovation, business development and building capacity for social impact endeavors Ability to translate regional technology trends and employer needs into applied programming, professional education, and academic partnerships Knowledge of applied AI, data analytics, and emerging-technology trends relevant to business, government, and healthcare sectors Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1307?c=uis": {"title": "Admission Counselor (Campus Based)-Two Vacancies", "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Admission Counselor (Campus Based)-Two Vacancies Springfield, IL, United States | 1005137 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/13/2026 Back to Search Admission Counselor (Campus Based)-Two Vacancies | Job Details Admission Counselor (Campus Based)-Two Vacancies Posting Category:\u00a0E About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs.  You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: Open Until Filled Minimum Starting Salary: $44,000.00 annually Summary: The admissions counselor position is responsible for recruiting and supporting new students at University of Illinois Springfield. This position represents the University at on- and off-campus events, including college fairs, school visits, daily campus visits, and large admissions programs. Counselors serve as key points of contact for school counselors, students, and families, providing guidance throughout the college search, admission, and enrollment process. The position requires strong communication and interpersonal skills to engage effectively with students, families, faculty, staff, and advisors. Responsibilities include delivering presentations to groups of varying sizes, conducting one-on-one meetings, and assisting with inquiries to ensure a positive experience for prospective students. This role plays a central part in shaping the first impressions of University of Illinois Springfield while supporting its enrollment goals through strategic outreach and personalized student support. Duties & Responsibilities: Outreach: 1. Attend school visits, college fairs, conferences, open houses, and other specialty events presenting to attendees. 2. Craft and execute targeted outreach plans in line with the enrollment strategy.\n3. Conduct webinars to increase knowledge of UIS as needed.\n4. Provide presentations to prospective students and families and provide tours as needed for prospective students and families. Recruitment: 1. Identifies, recruits and enrolls prospective undergraduate and graduate students within an assigned territory. 2. Develops and maintains relationships with prospective students and their support systems from the inquiry stage throughout the admissions funnel utilizing various communication tactics and platforms, including phone calls, video conferencing, and written correspondence. 3. Craft and execute targeted recruitment plans in line with the enrollment strategy. Application Review: Read and evaluate admissions applications, using a holistic view of each applicant to make decisions that align with our campus's enrollment targets. Partnership Outreach - Develops and maintains relationships with high school counselors, community college advisors, and college career counselors, providing timely updates and support for them and their students. Other: 1. Assist with admissions operational functions. 2. Engage in developing and executing communication campaigns, search committees, and various on-campus initiatives.\u00a0 3. Actively participate and contribute to relevant professional organizations.\n4. Join various admissions-related projects and tasks as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Bachelor\u2019s degree 2. Valid driver\u2019s license 3. Ability to present to both large and small groups 4. Ability to work independently and cooperatively with external and internal partners 5. Excellent oral and written communication skills 6. Excellent organizational and time management skills 7.Proficiency in general office software, such as word processing, spreadsheets, email, etc 8. Ability to travel overnight and work a flexible schedule including some early mornings, late evenings, and weekends when required. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Experience presenting to audiences 2. Experience with Technolutions Slate CRM 3. Bilingual Spanish/English. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Ability to work independently and collaboratively Excellent oral and written communication skills Excellent organizational and time management skills Proficiency in general office software, such as word processing, spreadsheets, email, etc Ability to travel overnight and work a flexible schedule including some evenings and weekends when required. Required abilities include speaking and hearing for in-person and virtual communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents or viewing screens, and performing tasks with repetitive fine motor skills. Physical Demands: Standing : Occasionally Walking : Occasionally Sitting : Frequently Lifting : Occasionally Carrying : Occasionally Pushing : Occasionally Pulling : Occasionally Climbing : Rarely Balancing : Rarely Stooping : Occasionally Kneeling : Rarely Crouching : Occasionally Crawling : Rarely Reaching : Occasionally Handling : Occasionally Grasping : Rarely Feeling : Rarely Talking : Constantly Hearing : Constantly Repetitive Motions : Rarely Eye/Hand/Foot Coordination : Rarely Taste/Smell : Rarely Performing Manual Tasks : Rarely Working Conditions: Extreme cold : Occasionally Extreme heat : Occasionally Humid : Occasionally Wet : Occasionally Noise : Constantly Hazards : Rarely Temperature Change : Rarely Atmospheric Conditions : Rarely Vibration : Rarely Travel Requirements: 40% Recruitment Travel Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.\u00a0 Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"}}, "rows": {"https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1336?c=uis": {"school_id": 412, "posting_url": "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1336?c=uis", "job_title_in_post": "Program Coordinator, Academic Governance and Institutional Effectiveness", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "10/5/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1270?c=uis": {"school_id": 412, "posting_url": "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1270?c=uis", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor, Public Management and Policy (MPP/MPA)", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Public Management and Policy; policy Evidence of teaching effectiveness", "deadline_of_application": "9/9/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1288?c=uis": {"school_id": 412, "posting_url": "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1288?c=uis", "job_title_in_post": "Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (up to 3 positions)", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Engineering Technology", "deadline_of_application": "9/3/2026", "position_start_date": "January 1, 2027"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1287?c=uis": {"school_id": 412, "posting_url": "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1287?c=uis", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (3 positions)", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Engineering Technology", "deadline_of_application": "9/3/2026", "position_start_date": "January 1, 2027"}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/868?c=uis": {"school_id": 412, "posting_url": "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/868?c=uis", "job_title_in_post": "Extra Help Event Attendant - 50 Vacancies", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "5/27/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1084?c=uis": {"school_id": 412, "posting_url": "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1084?c=uis", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct (Per Course) Teaching Opportunities", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "Center for Online Learning, Research and Service", "area_key_words": "Opportunities Posting Category", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/869?c=uis": {"school_id": 412, "posting_url": "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/869?c=uis", "job_title_in_post": "Extra Help Stagehand - 50 vacancies", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "9/6/2024", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/840?c=uis": {"school_id": 412, "posting_url": "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/840?c=uis", "job_title_in_post": "ION Instructor (per course)", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "ION; fully online classroom", "deadline_of_application": "8/6/2024", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1